{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401459-how-to-get-vampires-really-riled-up-against-mages","id":1401459,"title":"How to get vampires really riled up against mages?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-07-07T04:53:53-07:00","id":1401459,"title":"How to get vampires really riled up against mages?","content":"So mages and vampires don't mix very well, but I am playing in game where there are mages and vampires and generally they don't interact much but they exist in the same area. Well some stuff happened and a mage murdered a vampire by insane cheese that mages are known for(just scry their location then in the middle of the day instant kill them). I don't particularly want to fight a maxed out mage(yeah this game isn't balanced at all, there are maxed out mages) but those mages need to pay for what they did. So I was thinking, if I want to get revenge I need to turn all the vampires of the city against them!<br /> <br /> I don't think it is particularly hard to make vampires dislike mages, but also they are extremely dangerous so I think most would be a bit hesitant, so I am wondering, what can I say to really get people riled up? I was thinking of saying it is a Masquerade issue, that the mages know of vampires living in the city and they are willing to murder people in their haven so we can't let them get away with it. Maybe hype up that they are a threat to entire Camarilla. Is that enough though? They made the person disappear during the day to try to hide it, so I could twist things and suggest the mages might be responsible for every disappearance that has ever happened. It is wod so people disappear all the time, but if you catch mages doing it once in secret, maybe they have done it before and no one knew? It could of happened right, someone just left one day and no one knows what happened to them, maybe it was a mage? Above board I know they killed the person but in character I just know they took the person away, so I could play on fears and say maybe they abducted them in order to study them and they are chopping up their body or something?<br /> <br /> I am just thinking here, anyone has any good ideas to really tweak other vampires to get them really upset at mages? Any angles to get them really made. I kind of want to get people riled up enough that they would be willing to go to war with the mages(though I am not sure that will actually happen). Anyway, any thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1926-lilitha","name":"Lilitha","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-07T05:34:25-07:00","id":1401466,"title":"","content":"Just say a Mage turned one of them into a Gardenchair if you do not have any Tremere in the area. That statement is if the sayer is mighty enough enough to make a vampire really angry because for vampires this is the same like for a Garou to ghoul or embrace a Kinfolk.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-07T05:43:27-07:00","id":1401468,"title":"","content":"Murder a rival and leave their ashes on the roof of their haven. Then tell everyone the Mage did it and they're clearly on a killing spree.<br /> Set the media and police on them to dig up as much dirt as you can and hopefully chase them out of town (or raise enough noise that the technocracy turn up and do it for you).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25078-brickman","name":"Brickman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-07T05:44:09-07:00","id":1401470,"title":"","content":"you can't,<br /> vampires don't go to war against mages, unless they are cornered and have no other choice,<br /> they'd sooner run than fight in this scenario,<br /> and most vampires won't care about that one vampire that got killed (vampires tend to blame the victims)<br /> <br /> if you want revenge on the mage, you'll have to do it through proxies,<br /> through mortal assassins, other mages or a deal with a demon/spirit etc<br /> <br /> you don't want the revenge to be traced back to you<br /> <br /> as for the gardenchair thing, it could rile up vampires, but in most cases, all they'll do is kill the gardenchair and won't do anything against the mage","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-07T05:49:04-07:00","id":1401471,"title":"","content":"Have you looked at or read Blood Treachery? Its practically a guide book for vamp vs mage warfare","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-07T07:37:20-07:00","id":1401480,"title":"","content":"Maxed out Mages? You mean ones with Arete up to 5 or more? At that point you may as well just chuck it up as a loss. A cabal of Mages with that high Arete are almost unbeatable alone- but the tactic you espouse of getting all the Vampires on a bloodhunt against them may work.<br /> <br /> In the assault gather a bunch of Brujah with high focuses centered on Celerity- depending on the Paradigm of the cabal in question, their offensive rotes may take awhile to conjure up- leaving them open for attack. Once the Brujah are in close range to the opponents and mobs, the Mages in question should get a +2 difficulty for casting any effects- which will practically make them minse meat for the advancing Brujah with potence.<br /> <br /> Next have some Toreador with Celerity run at high speeds to quickly flank the cabal and make sure they are equipped with submachineguns and assault rifles- then do burst fire. Unless they have active Effects to harden their clothes as armor with Matter or their skin with Life, they are practically dead by that volley alone. <br /> <br /> To mop up the rest of the cabal, have units composed lead by one Nosferatu with lvl. 5 Obfuscate each so it can cover the whole group with Obfuscation, then have those kill squad units be a mix of Brujah with high Potence and Gangrel with Feral Claws from Protean lvl. 2 to kill silently kill the rest before they can react. Mages caught off guard are the easiest to kill. If they have high Mind they will already know your coming, but by then it will be already too late.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-07T07:59:30-07:00","id":1401481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401459-how-to-get-vampires-really-riled-up-against-mages?p=1401471#post1401471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you looked at or read Blood Treachery? Its practically a guide book for vamp vs mage warfare</div> </div> </div> </div>Definetly worth look up Blood Treachery - also how big a conflict do you want? Small local thing, or all the way up to the next act of the Massasa War?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26145-babi_gog","name":"babi_gog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-07T08:30:10-07:00","id":1401488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lilitha</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think it is particularly hard to make vampires dislike mages, but also they are extremely dangerous so I think most would be a bit hesitant, so I am wondering, what can I say to really get people riled up? I was thinking of saying it is a Masquerade issue, that the mages know of vampires living in the city and they are willing to murder people in their haven so we can't let them get away with it. Maybe hype up that they are a threat to entire Camarilla. Is that enough though? They made the person disappear during the day to try to hide it, so I could twist things and suggest the mages might be responsible for every disappearance that has ever happened. It is wod so people disappear all the time, but if you catch mages doing it once in secret, maybe they have done it before and no one knew? It could of happened right, someone just left one day and no one knows what happened to them, maybe it was a mage? Above board I know they killed the person but in character I just know they took the person away, so I could play on fears and say maybe they abducted them in order to study them and they are chopping up their body or something?</div> </div> </div> </div>While I agree that to give the mages bad press it's a good idea, I also think the question that's going to pop up in nearly every vampire's head it's: What do *I* get if I do this?<br /> <br /> Vampires in general aren't very altruistic, and don't trust other vampires. If the mages are obviously powerful then few are going to move (worse, may tip the mages against you) unless it's clearly in their best interest to follow your plans for some reason","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-07T11:13:43-07:00","id":1401517,"title":"","content":"One angle to consider may be, rather than just killing other vampires, convince your local Kindred that they are hunting them for magical components or lab rats for experiments. Tricky to actually pull off, but it makes the Mages come across more as an active and indiscriminate threat. There is also history; the Tremere literally began pulling similar stunts, and Vitae is noted as being a particular dark and death-tainted kind of Tass, in Mage terms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-07T11:16:15-07:00","id":1401518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>babi_gog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401459-how-to-get-vampires-really-riled-up-against-mages?p=1401481#post1401481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Definetly worth look up Blood Treachery - also how big a conflict do you want? Small local thing, or all the way up to the next act of the Massasa War?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well I don't really want to start up a war per say. At least in my mind, there seems like a tacit agreement that vampires and mages generally avoid each other and there are some mages working with some vampires. I can't actually tell which mage killed this vampire, because they did it at a distance without being seen or what not, I just know it involved mage magic. So my ideal outcome is that the mages of the city go, &quot;Oh crap this idiot really riled up all these vampires by murdering that guy is his haven! And then punish him or turn him over to us, or agree to not interfere in what happens next(being I just go in and kill that person myself). I think I could get the drop on them and kill them, but aside from it being crazy dangerous, I also want to avoid all his mage friends retaliating against me. I also want to avoid other vampires retaliating against me as well, since I can see some going, &quot;Why did you attack a mage, you are drawing too much attention now you got to go!&quot; or something like that.<br /> <br /> Anyway, getting the rest of the vampires really riled up seem like the best way to get support for anything related to going against the mages. There is also safety in numbers, which is kind of why the camarilla exists in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1926-lilitha","name":"Lilitha","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-07T11:37:00-07:00","id":1401522,"title":"","content":"<i>Blood Treachery</i> doesn't start as a war. A few Order of Hermes mages decide to start taking out Tremere vampires to gain magical power. Everything snowballs from there, but this is <i>Mage Revised </i>where the Order of Hermes and other mages have to work hard for power.<br /> <br /> So, the question is better answered with more details on the mages. Who are their allies? Who are their servants? Who are their enemies? Mages, unless you're in a zone of reality which they control, want to keep from being noticed just like vampires following the Masquerade.<br /> <br /> As for mages casting spells into the vampire's haven, what countermeasures do the vampires have to this magic? Mages can't always win by magic--there are a lot of ways to counterspell them, and there are Night Folk resistance rules in Mage 20.<br /> <br /> I would not expect mages to sell out a fellow mage. Perhaps aiming for compensation for the dead vampire-<i>wergilt </i>and an oath to leave town or not attack your character are more plausible. I mean, you're a vampire--to many mages you're an abomination. To those who don't see vampires as abominations, you're not part of their group.<br /> <br /> So, your character needs to know more about the mages in town and what they do. Now, if the problem is the Storyteller has powerful mages in game and is throwing their weight around, well then it might be best to play a different game.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-07T11:50:26-07:00","id":1401523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lilitha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401459-how-to-get-vampires-really-riled-up-against-mages?p=1401518#post1401518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, getting the rest of the vampires really riled up seem like the best way to get support for anything related to going against the mages. There is also safety in numbers, which is kind of why the camarilla exists in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>um no, that's not how it works,<br /> the best you can expect from the camarilla is the Tremere helping you...for a price (unless the mage is a common enemy of theirs...in which case they'll still feign ignorance to exploit you)<br /> <br /> and even then, you'll still be the one arranging for the killing,<br /> a Tremere may point you towards your target, even help you with some trinket or ritual or whatever,<br /> but getting a Tremere to do the killing for you is gonna require alot of pull","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-07T12:10:17-07:00","id":1401530,"title":"","content":"If it's obvious that the Mages are a threat to the Kindred as a whole, someone not helping is going to hurt them politically. Vampires are a lot like humans: individually treacherous, yet very judgey as a community when anyone else is caught being obviously treacherous or disloyal. If blatant, public disloyalty was acceptable in vampire society, sects couldn't even exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-07T12:18:31-07:00","id":1401531,"title":"","content":"Well the Tremere are already onboard, since it was a Tremere that got murdered. The problem is the rest of the vampires, who might just say, &quot;Well sounds like a Tremere problem&quot;. Or whatever. Well I want to frame it so it isn't a Tremere problem but a vampire problem, so other people get onboard as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1926-lilitha","name":"Lilitha","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-07T12:33:06-07:00","id":1401536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lilitha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401459-how-to-get-vampires-really-riled-up-against-mages?p=1401531#post1401531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well the Tremere are already onboard, since it was a Tremere that got murdered. The problem is the rest of the vampires, who might just say, &quot;Well sounds like a Tremere problem&quot;. Or whatever. Well I want to frame it so it isn't a Tremere problem but a vampire problem, so other people get onboard as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tremere can get them on board by just promising to repay the favour (tremere services are valuable),<br /> or they could threaten to stop providing service to those that rely on them<br /> <br /> getting others on board from the kindness of their heart would be a huge stretch,<br /> <br /> the mage would have to be a threat to the masquerade or murder vampires regularly to make it a camarilla problem (and even then, they may just decide to vacate the city...which the camarilla often does when facing a major supernatural threat such as lupines, hunters or mages)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-07T12:51:55-07:00","id":1401542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lilitha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401459-how-to-get-vampires-really-riled-up-against-mages?p=1401531#post1401531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well the Tremere are already onboard, since it was a Tremere that got murdered. The problem is the rest of the vampires, who might just say, &quot;Well sounds like a Tremere problem&quot;. Or whatever. Well I want to frame it so it isn't a Tremere problem but a vampire problem, so other people get onboard as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe they could lie to the local kindred that it <i>is </i>a vampire problem. First of all, mages are capable of doing terrible things, such as that murder. They also have powerful conspiracies. I wouldn't expect many kindred to know it, but one of them is literally called New World Order.<br /> That by itself probably wouldn't be enough, but by establishing it in everybody's imagination, one could tell all sorts of horror stories about what the mages are doing and they wouldn't neceassarily believe each one without proof, but they could still accept the mages <i>could </i>have done it. If this is V5, one could try blaming them for the Second Inquisition.<br /> Actually carrying out a witch hunt would be another matter. Then the local kindred need to believe that the local mages are weak enough to safely target, but also enough of a threat to be worth the trouble.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-07T13:06:12-07:00","id":1401545,"title":"","content":"This also depends what part of the Ascension War this cabal of Mages are, but I will assume they are either Tradition or Disparate since the Technocracy doesn't go by &quot;Mage&quot;- only Enlightened(?) individual. Solution: get the Technocracy involved. Despite the Technocracy's apparent goal of stroking out all reality deviation, their main focus are the other Awakened that don't toe their ideological line (Awakened being the term for a Human who isn't technically &quot;human&quot; anymore since they can use Magik/Enlightened procedures) so the Kindred can use that to their advantage, having the Technocracy deal with the Mages for you. Though if the Technocracy fails (which is likely since maxed out Arete Tradition or Disparate are different beasts cut from the rabble the Technocracy cleans up) or the Kindred can't contact or get the Technocracy to divert resources for such a small town, they'll have to fight the cabal themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-07T14:14:56-07:00","id":1401554,"title":"","content":"I think the truth may be the best option. Sure, vampires are likely to avoid war with mages as much as possible, and they won't care too much about this dead guy in particular. But I think they will care that someone has the capability of hunting down their lairs and exposing and killing them during the day. This is the sort of thing the Masquerade is meant to protect them from.<br /> <br /> So I think if your character goes at it from that angle: &quot;They could target any of us next!&quot; That might be enough to convince at least some of the vampires that it's in their best interest to see this threat dealt with. <br /> <br /> I think you'd have the best luck though if you've already done the legwork for them. Vampires might not be enthused about using their own manpower to target some lowly mages, but if you go in there with all the information at hand and it's just a matter of going and eliminating the threat, they might be more on board.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-07T19:23:30-07:00","id":1401596,"title":"","content":"Well, if it's a Tremere that got whacked, the mage threat level is up. Blood Treachery begins with the Tremere getting hit and they bring in the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> That being said, Act 4 of<i> Blood Treachery </i>has a lot of good stuff to get the fight going (the overall structure of the book is like a play).<br /> <br /> Frankly though, any vampire who has a mage who can take out a Tremere inside their haven from a distance with magic might be best working out a deal. Or roll up a new character and stay out of the pool of wizards, for they are not to be trifled with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-07T20:50:22-07:00","id":1401611,"title":"","content":"First thing I\u2019d look at is \u201cWhy did the mages choose to murder this particular vampire?\u201d<br /> <br /> Because if they\u2019re doing the research and risking the paradox to hit a Tremere in their own haven, it\u2019s not just a random killing. Did the vampire do something to one of the mages or their loved ones? Did the vampire have something the mages wanted or needed? <br /> <br /> Figure out what the mages want and you might be able to make them your tool against enemy vampires and that is way more useful than just trying to kill them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T01:41:20-07:00","id":1401639,"title":"","content":"Also thinking if it was the Tremere who where targeted, then it is possible (depending on the political make up of the local kindred) that this may be seen as a &quot;<i>good thing</i>&quot;, and &quot;<i>oh what a pity</i>&quot;. There is also the possibility that the mages where hired by other kindred to do this...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26145-babi_gog","name":"babi_gog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T07:48:33-07:00","id":1401691,"title":"","content":"Mages with time magic start calling vampires, to spoil the vampires anticipation of the outcome of a game. &quot;Oh, you wanna watch the Bull v Spurs game? Well, the Bull's do goo until the 4th quarter and then they choke...&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}